# Opalescence's ruling: "A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be
# activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent
# turn. It doesn't matter how long the permanent has been a creature" (CR 302.6). Bot1's Bow of Nylea came on turn 1; on
# turn 3 Opalescence makes it a 3/3 creature that very turn, and Bot1 may still activate "{1}{G}, {T}: ... You gain 3 life"
# - Bot1 goes to 23. Bot2's Bow of Nylea, cast on turn 4 while Opalescence is out, is a creature that has not been under
# Bot2's control since its turn began, so with {1}{G} open its {T} ability is not offered (the refusal).

